{"name":"Barrel Sponge","hex":"#9e3c31","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barrel sponge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sponge of the genus Xestospongia, especially Xestospongia testudinaria."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel_sponge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel","wikidata":"Q10289"},{"title":"Sponge","blocks":[{"text":"Sponges or sea sponges are primarily marine invertebrates of the animal phylum Porifera. They are filter feeders that are typically bound to the seabed, being sessile. Sponges are one of the most ancient members of living seabed community (macrobenthos), with many species being important reef-builders. Some sponge species inhabit freshwater."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sponges_in_Caribbean_Sea%2C_Cayman_Islands.jpg/330px-Sponges_in_Caribbean_Sea%2C_Cayman_Islands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sponge","wikidata":"Q18960"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg/500px-Mackmyra_Whisky_-_Warehouse_Whisky_barrels_at_Hackeberga_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76